<Wiki
  title="puv tool"
  description="Install a global tool in its own environment, with a shim on PATH."
>
  <p class="kicker">Wiki</p>
  <h1>tool</h1>
  <p>
    <code>puv tool install</code> installs a global tool. Like
    <a href="/wiki/commands/load"><code>puv load</code></a>, the tool gets its own environment
    and does not share the application solve. Unlike <code>load</code>, it is not tied to one
    project.
  </p>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <pre class="block">puv tool install phpstan/phpstan</pre>
  <p>
    The environment is stored under <code>~/.local/share/puv/</code> with the other global tools.
    A shim is written to <code>~/.local/bin</code>. <code>PUV_BIN_DIR</code> moves that shim
    directory. <code>PUV_DATA_DIR</code> moves the environment. Both are listed on
    <a href="/wiki/files">files</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Project-local instead</h2>
  <pre class="block">puv load phpstan/phpstan</pre>
  <p>
    Use <code>load</code> when the tool should travel with the project, under
    <code>.puv/tools/</code>, and <code>tool install</code> when every project on the machine
    should see the shim.
  </p>
</Wiki>
